ure on this diagonal and now d5 now  the queen also helps out with the  defense of the f7 pawn f5 trying to bust  open the position and now bishop to a6  attacking the rook on f1 f captures on  e6 opening up the position and here mr  king just castles queen side  uh rook captures on f7 attacking the  black queen here and now queen c to a5  uh bishop to e7 and it's still a very  interesting game but after queen to a5  there's just not all that much for black  to do however uh this is uh like we said  a fabrication and we need more queens  than the board c3 attacking the queen on  b4 queen to d6 and now bishop to g4  threatening all sorts of nasty  discoveries so if e7 then okay you lose  too much material so here rook to e8 was  played but now just pawn to e7 with  check we have king to b8 and now e  captures an f8 bringing a fourth queen  into the game for white uh and the  seventh queen in total yeah and in this  uh sort of fabricated game it was in  this position on move 30 that uh mr king  resigned the game as there is nothing  more to be done here but just uh i'll  show you what would happen uh i mean  look at all this firepower attacking the  rook here let's say you take one queen  of the board it doesn't really matter  queen captures an f8 queen captures rook  captures and that's it now you're  getting checkmated not much for you to  do here you're gonna deliver a check now  yeah the king has to go back somewhere  on the on the sixth rank king to c6  queen to e8 with check and now after  king d6 is just a nice mate in one queen  to d7 with the check or queen the e6  would check or you know you can pretty  much do anything and still win the game  but yeah in on move 30 after he captures  on a faith promoting to a queen and mr  king resigned and what uh what a  wonderful game uh finishing uh with a  position of seven queens on the board so  really really incredible but uh not as  incredible as the revelation at least  for me that it was not arpadillo who uh  inv